{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "PV soiling and cleaning study (template)",
  "notes": "Template for a field study at a ground-mounted PV plant in a dusty, semi-arid location. Each run is one string of modules over one cleaning cycle. Cleaning interval, cleaning method and an anti-soiling coating are set per string; rainfall since the last cleaning, mean PM10 concentration and mean module temperature are recorded from the on-site weather station. Performance ratio and soiling loss come from the string monitoring compared with a reference string cleaned daily. Choose a design on the Design page (an optimal design with environmental interactions suits a study over one dry season).",
